<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:bioc="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn/biocolor/1.0" xmlns:color="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/non-normative/color/1.0" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_1ksue5u" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.22.0" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.4.0">
  <bpmn:process id="Process_OrderCreated" name="ACME_Picking_OrderCreated" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Workflow 100: Triggered by picking.order.create signal.
Checks whether ALL order items are available in the Z2 picking zone (aisles 01-14).
If yes: sets order data.status="fulfillable" + data.statusAt=timestamp.
If no: logs unavailable items (host notification placeholder), waits 1h, retries indefinitely.

GOTCHA: Availability is checked via item.data.storageSlots (not Pyck stock model).
The host system cannot export per-location stock quantities, so we track which
locations an article is assigned to (from StorageSlots.json) but not how many units
are at each location. An item is "available in Z2" if it has at least one
storage-slot entry with zone=="Z2".

GOTCHA: A few articles have no storageSlots at all (orphaned in host system).
Orders containing these items will loop indefinitely until the data is fixed.

GOTCHA: No retry limit on the hourly loop. The workflow will run forever for
permanently unavailable items. Consider adding a max retry / timeout later.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_1" name="Picking Order&#10;Created">
      <bpmn:documentation>Signal: picking.order.create
Input: PickingOrder ID from the signal payload.
The order must have dataTypeSlug=acme-picking-order with order items
using dataTypeSlug=acme-picking-order-item.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_0r6hzjx</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_0r6hzjx" sourceRef="StartEvent_1" targetRef="Activity_1h7v8uq" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_1h7v8uq" name="Check ALL order items available in Zone Z2">
      <bpmn:documentation>Activity: CheckItemAvailability

1. Fetch the picking order and its order items (relay connection).
2. For each order item, resolve the inventory item by SKU.
3. Read item.data.storageSlots array.
4. Check if ANY entry has zone=="Z2".
5. ALL items must pass for the order to be available.

Returns: { available: bool, missingItems: []string }

SCOPE: Only Zone Z2 (aisles 01-14). Other picking zones (Z1, Z3) are excluded.
DEFINITION: Available = every order item has at least one storage slot in Z2. Partial availability is NOT sufficient.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_0r6hzjx</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_0m830hg</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_0pg7szv</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_0xcskz4" name="All items&#10;available?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_0pg7szv</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1p31hon</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1uugdk4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_0pg7szv" sourceRef="Activity_1h7v8uq" targetRef="Gateway_0xcskz4" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1p31hon" name="No" sourceRef="Gateway_0xcskz4" targetRef="Activity_001b069" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1lqokom" sourceRef="Activity_001b069" targetRef="Event_0hj0xec" />
    <bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent id="Event_0hj0xec" name="Wait 1 hour">
      <bpmn:documentation>Temporal: workflow.Sleep(ctx, 1*time.Hour)
No retry limit -- loops indefinitely until all items are available.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1lqokom</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_0m830hg</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:timerEventDefinition id="TimerEventDefinition_1aqfhkg" />
    </bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_0m830hg" sourceRef="Event_0hj0xec" targetRef="Activity_1h7v8uq" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_001b069" name="Log unavailable items (host notification placeholder)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Activity: NotifyHostUnavailable

Currently a placeholder: logs which items are missing from Z2.
Format: "Order {extOrderNo}: items unavailable in Z2: [{sku1}, {sku2}]"

TODO: Replace with actual host system notification (webhook/API call)
when the integration endpoint is defined.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1p31hon</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1lqokom</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_1jcm9kt" name="Mark order as fulfillable">
      <bpmn:documentation>Activity: MarkOrderFulfillable

Updates the picking order's data field:
  data.status = "fulfillable"
  data.statusAt = current ISO timestamp

Uses: updatePickingOrder mutation with dataTypeSlug=acme-picking-order.
The tour-creation workflow (101) queries orders where data.status=="fulfillable".</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1uugdk4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_14ybmli</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1uugdk4" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gateway_0xcskz4" targetRef="Activity_1jcm9kt" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_0icc7ya" name="Order fulfillable">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_14ybmli</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_14ybmli" sourceRef="Activity_1jcm9kt" targetRef="Event_0icc7ya" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_scope">
      <bpmn:text>Scope: Zone Z2 only (aisles 01-14)
Check: item.data.storageSlots.any(zone=="Z2")
NOT using Pyck stock model (host can't export per-location qty)</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Association_scope" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Activity_1h7v8uq" targetRef="TextAnnotation_scope" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_retry">
      <bpmn:text>No retry limit -- loops hourly until available.
Orphaned articles (no storageSlots) will block forever.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Association_retry" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Event_0hj0xec" targetRef="TextAnnotation_retry" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_fulfill">
      <bpmn:text>Sets data.status="fulfillable" + data.statusAt on the order.
Tour-creation workflow (101) queries this status.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Association_fulfill" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Activity_1jcm9kt" targetRef="TextAnnotation_fulfill" />
  </bpmn:process>
